# Robinhood MCP Guardrails

Apply when using **Robinhood Trading MCP** (`https://agent.robinhood.com/mcp/trading`) or when the user mentions Robinhood positions, Agentic account, or MCP portfolio data.

If MCP tools fail with **-32600 / structured content**, confirm `.cursor/mcp.json` matches [mcp.json.example](../mcp.json.example) (proxy + `mcp-remote`). See [mcp-cursor-compat.md](../../project-docs/reference/mcp-cursor-compat.md).

## Read vs trade

| Action | Allowed |
|--------|---------|
| List accounts, positions, balances, order history | All accounts (discovery OK) |
| Place/modify/cancel orders | **Robinhood Agentic (C) only** |
| Trades on IRA or taxable via MCP | **Never** |

## Phase gate

**No autonomous execution before Phase 3B** ([PROJECT.md](PROJECT.md)). Co-pilot: user `confirm` before place.

- Default: **read-only** MCP usage until an explicit co-pilot confirm.
- Do not invoke order-placement MCP tools unless the user confirms the plan.
- After any Agentic (C) trade: log to `trader-memory-core` via `thesis_store.py` / `/log-positions`.

## Portfolio B (IRA)

- May appear in MCP account lists — **do not log** IRA positions or run four-questions.
- Do not spend session time on IRA eligibility workflows unless the user explicitly asks about IRA.

## Thesis logging (A + C only)

- Never write YAML directly under `state/theses/`.
- Use [commands/log-positions.md](commands/log-positions.md) or `thesis_store.py` / thesis-manager.
- Sources: `state/pending_ingest.json` (Portfolio A sync) or MCP snapshot for **Agentic (C)** / taxable (A).
- Skip `ira_robinhood` rows.

## Hybrid with scripts

- Daily market: `uv run python3 scripts/pre_market.py` (not MCP).
- Scheduled taxable sync: `robinhood_sync.py` + timer — keep for Portfolio A.

## Account keys

| Portfolio | `thesis_store` account | In scope |
|-----------|------------------------|----------|
| A taxable | `robinhood_taxable` | Sync + log |
| B IRA | `ira_robinhood` | Discover only — no log |
| C Agentic | `robinhood_agentic` | Trade + log |

See account discovery table in [decisions.md](decisions.md).
